,"text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Scale-Up"},{"type":"h","text":"Quality"},{"type":"p","text":"GMP"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Quality Control"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Microbial Quality"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Documentation"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Stability"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Regulatory Awareness"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"p","text":"Excel"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Statistics"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"DoE"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"LIMS"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"QMS"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Data Analysis"}]},{"heading":"Target Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should ideally have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strong cosmetic formulation knowledge"},{"text":"Strong pharmaceutics fundamentals"},{"text":"Knowledge of cosmetic ingredients"},{"text":"Emulsion and surfactant expertise"},{"text":"Practical formulation experience"},{"text":"Stability-testing experience"},{"text":"Basic microbiological knowledge"},{"text":"GMP knowledge"},{"text":"Product-development documentation skills"},{"text":"Packaging compatibility awareness"},{"text":"Basic regulatory knowledge"},{"text":"Excel/statistical skills"},{"text":"At least one substantial cosmetic formulation project"},{"text":"Relevant cosmetic R&D internship"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"B.Pharm"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Cosmetic Formulation Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Ingredient Knowledge"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Cosmetic R&D Internship"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"3–5 Prototype Formulations"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Stability Study"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Product Development Project"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"GMP / Quality Knowledge"},{"type":"p","text":"+"},{"type":"flow","items":["Excel + Basic DoE","Product Development Trainee","Cosmetic Product Developer"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Pharm","Cosmetic formulation specialization","hands-on R&D internship","portfolio of formulation prototypes","Product Development Trainee","Cosmetic Product Developer","Senior Formulation/Product Development Specialist","Product Development Manager"]},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, the strongest differentiator is the ability to formulate and troubleshoot real products, not simply having a pharmacy degree. A graduate who can explain why each ingredient is selected, how the formulation is optimized, how stability is assessed, and how the product moves from laboratory prototype to commercial scale will have a substantially stronger profile."}]}]}